1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,655
In May 2008, a man in
Las Vegas called 911.

2
00:00:04,972 --> 00:00:08,688
His wife had been shot,
he said, by a masked intruder.

3
00:00:09,043 --> 00:00:11,170
And he said something else.

4
00:00:11,564 --> 00:00:14,873
He'd wrestled the gun away
from the man, and shot him.

5
00:00:15,712 --> 00:00:18,526
The man he shot wasn't a stranger.

6
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:20,460
He was Michael Miller,

7
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:23,211
a thirty-eight-year-old
handyman the caller knew.

8
00:00:23,546 --> 00:00:25,906
The caller was Thomas Randolph.

9
00:00:26,228 --> 00:00:28,976
And Sharon, his sixth wife, was dead.

10
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:33,312
Prosecutors would later tell
a jury a very different story.

11
00:00:33,691 --> 00:00:36,903
They alleged Randolph had
hired Miller to kill Sharon,

12
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:39,259
then shot Miller to silence a witness.

13
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:41,828
Randolph says he's innocent.

14
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:45,275
He has now stood trial
for murder three times.

15
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,774
One jury acquitted him.

16
00:00:48,113 --> 00:00:50,376
Two juries convicted him.

17
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:55,509
And the first of those convictions, with
its two death sentences, was thrown out,

18
00:00:55,509 --> 00:00:59,433
because the jury had heard about a
death he'd already been acquitted of.

19
00:01:00,011 --> 00:01:03,763
To understand how that happened,
we have to go back to Utah,

20
00:01:03,763 --> 00:01:06,606
more than twenty years
before that 911 call.

21
00:01:06,994 --> 00:01:10,119
This is the true story
behind Netflix's The Widower,

22
00:01:10,119 --> 00:01:12,221
and where Thomas Randolph is now.

23
00:01:14,964 --> 00:01:18,224
Thomas Randolph has
been married six times.

24
00:01:18,499 --> 00:01:23,070
His first marriage
lasted from 1975 to 1983.

25
00:01:23,327 --> 00:01:27,653
That wife is still alive, and years
later, she testified against him.

26
00:01:27,896 --> 00:01:30,888
In 1983 he married Becky Gault.

27
00:01:31,237 --> 00:01:35,340
According to reports, it was the
same day his divorce came through.

28
00:01:35,629 --> 00:01:38,429
After Becky, there were
four more marriages.

29
00:01:38,902 --> 00:01:41,567
Four of his six wives have died.

30
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:46,821
But those deaths were very different, and
the law has treated them very differently.

31
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:51,577
One died in 2004, after heart surgery.

32
00:01:52,097 --> 00:01:54,207
Another died of cancer.

33
00:01:54,713 --> 00:01:57,503
He was never charged over either death.

34
00:01:58,230 --> 00:02:01,142
One, in Utah, led to a murder trial.

35
00:02:01,459 --> 00:02:05,537
And one, in Las Vegas, led to
the sentence he's serving now.

36
00:02:05,804 --> 00:02:06,804
Utah.

37
00:02:07,037 --> 00:02:09,778
November 1986.

38
00:02:10,203 --> 00:02:14,711
Becky Gault, Randolph's second wife,
died at home from a gunshot wound.

39
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:18,099
At first, her death was ruled a suicide.

40
00:02:18,413 --> 00:02:23,308
Then a former friend and co-worker,
Eric Tarantino, went to the authorities.

41
00:02:23,752 --> 00:02:27,202
He told them Randolph had talked
about having Becky killed,

42
00:02:27,202 --> 00:02:28,794
for the insurance money.

43
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:31,959
Randolph was charged with her murder.

44
00:02:32,283 --> 00:02:36,407
And while he sat in jail waiting for
trial, according to news reports,

45
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:40,531
he offered a cellmate cash, and the
title to a car, to kill Tarantino.

46
00:02:41,435 --> 00:02:44,761
The cellmate was an
undercover police officer.

47
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:49,089
Randolph pleaded guilty to
felony witness tampering.

48
00:02:49,343 --> 00:02:52,055
The murder charge was a different story.

49
00:02:52,442 --> 00:02:57,596
At trial in 1989, his lawyers argued
that Becky had taken her own life.

50
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,619
And the jury acquitted him.

51
00:03:01,259 --> 00:03:03,222
Remember that acquittal.

52
00:03:03,741 --> 00:03:08,274
Three decades later, in a courtroom
in Las Vegas, it would matter again.

53
00:03:08,956 --> 00:03:14,036
By 2008, Randolph was living in Las
Vegas with his sixth wife, Sharon.

54
00:03:14,437 --> 00:03:19,516
Prosecutors would later say he'd taken out
life insurance on Sharon in the two years

55
00:03:19,516 --> 00:03:23,072
before she died, and stood to
collect more than $300,000.

56
00:03:23,485 --> 00:03:26,894
Investigators went through
the phone records, too.

57
00:03:27,336 --> 00:03:30,104
They counted nearly 300
calls between Randolph

58
00:03:30,104 --> 00:03:32,872
and Miller in the months
before the shootings.

59
00:03:33,225 --> 00:03:36,109
Most, they said, were made by Randolph.

60
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:40,703
Randolph told police Miller was
wearing a mask when he shot him.

61
00:03:41,568 --> 00:03:44,856
But police said Miller had
been shot in the forehead.

62
00:03:45,323 --> 00:03:49,425
And the ski mask was found on the
garage floor, with no blood on it,

63
00:03:49,425 --> 00:03:50,866
and no bullet holes.

64
00:03:51,421 --> 00:03:54,329
Then there was the 911 call itself.

65
00:03:54,776 --> 00:04:00,854
Prosecutors said the dispatcher had to ask
Randolph several times to give Sharon CPR.

66
00:04:01,219 --> 00:04:04,037
His defence argued the
call showed something else:

67
00:04:04,037 --> 00:04:08,565
a man screaming and crying over his wife,
and the only person who tried to help her.

68
00:04:08,885 --> 00:04:12,837
Detectives also filmed Randolph
walking them through the house.

69
00:04:13,218 --> 00:04:17,194
On that video, he acts out the
shootings and, one station reported,

70
00:04:17,194 --> 00:04:19,264
mimics the sound of the gunfire.

71
00:04:19,702 --> 00:04:22,767
Jurors at both of his
trials would watch it.

72
00:04:23,029 --> 00:04:26,579
His defence argued there was no
physical evidence of any plot,

73
00:04:26,579 --> 00:04:29,972
and that Miller acted alone,
in a burglary that went wrong.

74
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:33,454
Eight months after the
shootings, in January 2009,

75
00:04:33,454 --> 00:04:37,587
police arrested Randolph at his
parents' home in Clearfield, Utah.

76
00:04:37,837 --> 00:04:39,445
He was fifty-three.

77
00:04:39,735 --> 00:04:43,873
He was charged with conspiracy to
commit murder, and with murder.

78
00:04:44,237 --> 00:04:46,092
And then, he waited.

79
00:04:46,542 --> 00:04:50,001
It would be almost nine
years before his first trial.

80
00:04:50,741 --> 00:04:55,169
In 2017, the case finally
went to trial in Las Vegas.

81
00:04:55,652 --> 00:04:58,893
And this time, the jury heard
about Utah: Becky's death,

82
00:04:58,893 --> 00:05:02,605
and witnesses who said Randolph
had tried to arrange her killing.

83
00:05:03,041 --> 00:05:06,696
Before that evidence could be
used, the judge held a hearing.

84
00:05:06,967 --> 00:05:09,342
The State called just one witness: the

85
00:05:09,342 --> 00:05:12,095
prosecutor from Randolph's
Utah murder trial.

86
00:05:12,902 --> 00:05:15,535
The jury heard all of it,
even though Randolph

87
00:05:15,535 --> 00:05:17,712
had been acquitted of Becky's murder.

88
00:05:18,346 --> 00:05:21,382
Two of his former wives testified, too.

89
00:05:22,165 --> 00:05:27,096
On the 28th of June, 2017, the jury
found Randolph guilty of conspiracy,

90
00:05:27,096 --> 00:05:30,067
and of two counts of first-degree murder.

91
00:05:30,763 --> 00:05:33,717
A week later, the same
jury, eight women and

92
00:05:33,717 --> 00:05:36,435
four men, sentenced him to death, twice.

93
00:05:36,953 --> 00:05:39,616
One sentence for each victim.

94
00:05:40,776 --> 00:05:41,934
He appealed.

95
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:46,909
And on the 10th of December, 2020,
the Nevada Supreme Court threw out the

96
00:05:46,909 --> 00:05:50,798
convictions and both death sentences,
and ordered a new trial.

97
00:05:51,358 --> 00:05:53,062
The reason was Utah.

98
00:05:53,327 --> 00:05:56,601
The court said that evidence
should never have been admitted,

99
00:05:56,601 --> 00:06:00,412
because the risk of unfair prejudice
substantially outweighed its value.

100
00:06:00,673 --> 00:06:05,523
It found the State's proof of those old
allegations rested on a single witness.

101
00:06:05,787 --> 00:06:08,782
And it pointed out that
Randolph had been acquitted.

102
00:06:09,185 --> 00:06:11,870
The ruling didn't mean he was innocent.

103
00:06:12,341 --> 00:06:14,781
It meant he'd be tried again.

104
00:06:15,432 --> 00:06:20,133
Two months later, Dateline NBC aired
a three-part series about the case.

105
00:06:20,385 --> 00:06:22,245
It was called The Widower.

106
00:06:22,561 --> 00:06:26,039
The retrial began in August 2023.

107
00:06:26,450 --> 00:06:28,935
This time, prosecutors
were largely limited

108
00:06:28,935 --> 00:06:31,420
to the deaths of Sharon
and Michael Miller.

109
00:06:31,742 --> 00:06:34,225
And they didn't seek the death penalty.

110
00:06:34,467 --> 00:06:38,749
Defence attorney Josh Tomsheck told the
jury there was no physical evidence of a

111
00:06:38,749 --> 00:06:41,188
plot, and that Randolph
was the only person

112
00:06:41,188 --> 00:06:43,279
who tried to help Sharon that night.

113
00:06:43,998 --> 00:06:47,132
The jury deliberated for
more than four hours.

114
00:06:47,571 --> 00:06:51,072
Then it found Randolph guilty
of conspiracy to commit murder,

115
00:06:51,072 --> 00:06:53,946
and of two counts of murder
with a deadly weapon.

116
00:06:54,603 --> 00:06:57,872
In April 2024, Judge
Tierra Jones sentenced

117
00:06:57,872 --> 00:07:00,741
him to sixty years to life in prison.

118
00:07:01,489 --> 00:07:04,424
At his sentencing, Randolph spoke.

119
00:07:05,266 --> 00:07:07,775
"I didn't kill Sharon," he said.

120
00:07:08,251 --> 00:07:10,584
"I have nothing to do with this."

121
00:07:11,321 --> 00:07:12,968
He appealed again.

122
00:07:13,373 --> 00:07:17,363
He argued that years of delay had
violated his right to a speedy trial,

123
00:07:17,363 --> 00:07:21,613
and that what he told detectives on
that walkthrough video wasn't voluntary.

124
00:07:22,418 --> 00:07:27,894
On the 31st of August, 2026, the Nevada
Supreme Court rejected every one of his

125
00:07:27,894 --> 00:07:30,728
arguments, and upheld the convictions.

126
00:07:31,272 --> 00:07:35,848
The nine years before his first trial,
it said, didn't violate his rights.

127
00:07:36,117 --> 00:07:40,314
The nineteen-month wait before the
retrial was long enough to be presumed

128
00:07:40,314 --> 00:07:42,917
prejudicial, but the
State wasn't to blame.

129
00:07:43,189 --> 00:07:47,992
He'd also said he was in pain, and on
medication, when he spoke to detectives.

130
00:07:48,282 --> 00:07:52,868
Two detectives testified otherwise,
and the court let his statements stand.

131
00:07:53,208 --> 00:07:56,098
Today, Thomas Randolph
is in his seventies,

132
00:07:56,098 --> 00:08:00,168
serving his sentence at Lovelock
Correctional Center in Nevada.

133
00:08:00,912 --> 00:08:02,974
He says he is innocent.

134
00:08:03,724 --> 00:08:07,009
One journalist had been
there almost from the start.

135
00:08:07,327 --> 00:08:11,868
Dateline producer Dan Slepian was
embedded with Las Vegas police in 2008,

136
00:08:11,868 --> 00:08:14,053
and followed the case for years.

137
00:08:14,478 --> 00:08:18,515
On the 30th of September, 2026,
Netflix released The Widower:

138
00:08:18,515 --> 00:08:21,708
'Til Death Do Us Part,
directed by Chris Smith.

139
00:08:21,992 --> 00:08:26,276
It follows Slepian, and Las Vegas
police detective Dean O'Kelley.

140
00:08:26,525 --> 00:08:29,488
In its first week,
it drew 11.6 million views,

141
00:08:29,488 --> 00:08:33,989
and was reported as Netflix's number-two
English-language film worldwide.

142
00:08:34,356 --> 00:08:36,991
So, here's where the record stands.

143
00:08:37,649 --> 00:08:42,411
In Utah, a jury acquitted Randolph
of murder in Becky Gault's death.

144
00:08:42,829 --> 00:08:45,699
He pleaded guilty to witness tampering.

145
00:08:46,429 --> 00:08:50,730
No charge was ever brought over the
deaths of two of his other wives.

146
00:08:51,439 --> 00:08:56,636
In Las Vegas, two juries convicted him
of murdering Sharon and Michael Miller.

147
00:08:57,072 --> 00:08:59,605
The first verdict was thrown out.

148
00:09:00,036 --> 00:09:02,223
The second has been upheld.

149
00:09:02,925 --> 00:09:05,989
Thomas Randolph says
he didn't kill Sharon.

150
00:09:06,482 --> 00:09:08,969
Two juries said that he did.
